The new reserved-word tests don’t currently cover `operationId: "await"`, which is reserved in ES modules and would still trigger the original syntax error if omitted from the reserved list. Adding a focused test case for `await` would prevent regressions once the reserved-word set is updated.
```suggestion

    it("appends underscore when operationId is await", () => {
      const coder = new OperationTypeCoder(
        new Requirement({ operationId: "await" }, "#/paths/stuff/get"),
        "get",
      );

      expect(coder.getOperationBaseName()).toBe("await_");
    });
```

